Grammar

    0 $accept: function $end

    1 function: function_header optional_variable body

    2 function_header: FUNCTION IDENTIFIER parameters RETURNS type ';'
    3                | FUNCTION error ';'

    4 parameters: parameter_list
    5           | ε

    6 parameter_list: parameter
    7               | parameter ',' parameter_list

    8 parameter: IDENTIFIER ':' type

    9 type: INTEGER
   10     | CHARACTER
   11     | REAL

   12 optional_variable: variable optional_variable
   13                  | ε

   14 variable: IDENTIFIER ':' type IS statement ';'
   15         | IDENTIFIER ':' LIST OF type IS list ';'
   16         | error ';'

   17 list: '(' expressions ')'

   18 expressions: expressions ',' expression
   19            | expression

   20 body: BEGIN_ statement_ END ';'

   21 statement_: statement ';'
   22           | error ';'

   23 statement: expression
   24          | WHEN condition ',' expression ':' expression
   25          | SWITCH expression IS cases OTHERS ARROW statement ';' ENDSWITCH
   26          | FOLD direction operator list_choice ENDFOLD
   27          | IF condition THEN statement_ elsif_statements else_statement ENDIF

   28 direction: LEFT
   29          | RIGHT

   30 operator: ADDOP
   31         | MULOP
   32         | REMOP

   33 list_choice: list
   34            | IDENTIFIER

   35 elsif_statements: elsif_statement elsif_statements
   36                 | ε

   37 elsif_statement: ELSIF condition THEN statement_

   38 else_statement: ELSE statement_
   39               | ε

   40 cases: cases case
   41      | ε

   42 case: CASE INT_LITERAL ARROW statement ';'
   43     | error ';'

   44 condition: condition OROP logical_and
   45          | logical_and

   46 logical_and: logical_and ANDOP relation
   47            | relation

   48 relation: '(' condition ')'
   49         | expression RELOP expression
   50         | NOTOP relation

   51 expression: expression ADDOP term
   52           | term

   53 term: term MULOP factor
   54     | term REMOP factor
   55     | factor

   56 factor: primary
   57       | primary EXPOP factor

   58 primary: '(' expression ')'
   59        | INT_LITERAL
   60        | CHAR_LITERAL
   61        | IDENTIFIER '(' expression ')'
   62        | IDENTIFIER
   63        | REAL_LITERAL
   64        | NEGOP primary


Terminals, with rules where they appear

    $end (0) 0
    '(' (40) 17 48 58 61
    ')' (41) 17 48 58 61
    ',' (44) 7 18 24
    ':' (58) 8 14 15 24
    ';' (59) 2 3 14 15 16 20 21 22 25 42 43
    error (256) 3 16 22 43
    IDENTIFIER <iden> (258) 2 8 14 15 34 61 62
    INT_LITERAL <type> (259) 42 59
    CHAR_LITERAL <type> (260) 60
    REAL_LITERAL <type> (261) 63
    ADDOP (262) 30 51
    MULOP (263) 31 53
    RELOP (264) 49
    ANDOP (265) 46
    ARROW (266) 25 42
    BEGIN_ (267) 20
    CASE (268) 42
    CHARACTER (269) 10
    ELSE (270) 38
    END (271) 20
    ENDSWITCH (272) 25
    FUNCTION (273) 2 3
    INTEGER (274) 9
    IS (275) 14 15 25
    LIST (276) 15
    OF (277) 15
    OTHERS (278) 25
    RETURNS (279) 2
    SWITCH (280) 25
    WHEN (281) 24
    ELSIF (282) 37
    ENDFOLD (283) 26
    ENDIF (284) 27
    FOLD (285) 26
    IF (286) 27
    LEFT (287) 28
    REAL (288) 11
    RIGHT (289) 29
    THEN (290) 27 37
    OROP (291) 44
    NOTOP (292) 50
    REMOP (293) 32 54
    EXPOP (294) 57
    NEGOP (295) 64


Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

    $accept (46)
        on left: 0
    function (47)
        on left: 1
        on right: 0
    function_header <type> (48)
        on left: 2 3
        on right: 1
    parameters (49)
        on left: 4 5
        on right: 2
    parameter_list (50)
        on left: 6 7
        on right: 4 7
    parameter (51)
        on left: 8
        on right: 6 7
    type <type> (52)
        on left: 9 10 11
        on right: 2 8 14 15
    optional_variable (53)
        on left: 12 13
        on right: 1 12
    variable (54)
        on left: 14 15 16
        on right: 12
    list <type> (55)
        on left: 17
        on right: 15 33
    expressions <type> (56)
        on left: 18 19
        on right: 17 18
    body <type> (57)
        on left: 20
        on right: 1
    statement_ <type> (58)
        on left: 21 22
        on right: 20 27 37 38
    statement <type> (59)
        on left: 23 24 25 26 27
        on right: 14 21 25 42
    direction (60)
        on left: 28 29
        on right: 26
    operator (61)
        on left: 30 31 32
        on right: 26
    list_choice <type> (62)
        on left: 33 34
        on right: 26
    elsif_statements <type> (63)
        on left: 35 36
        on right: 27 35
    elsif_statement <type> (64)
        on left: 37
        on right: 35
    else_statement <type> (65)
        on left: 38 39
        on right: 27
    cases <type> (66)
        on left: 40 41
        on right: 25 40
    case <type> (67)
        on left: 42 43
        on right: 40
    condition (68)
        on left: 44 45
        on right: 24 27 37 44 48
    logical_and (69)
        on left: 46 47
        on right: 44 45 46
    relation (70)
        on left: 48 49 50
        on right: 46 47 50
    expression <type> (71)
        on left: 51 52
        on right: 18 19 23 24 25 49 51 58 61
    term <type> (72)
        on left: 53 54 55
        on right: 51 52 53 54
    factor <type> (73)
        on left: 56 57
        on right: 53 54 55 57
    primary <type> (74)
        on left: 58 59 60 61 62 63 64
        on right: 56 57 64


State 0

    0 $accept: • function $end

    FUNCTION  shift, and go to state 1

    function         go to state 2
    function_header  go to state 3


State 1

    2 function_header: FUNCTION • IDENTIFIER parameters RETURNS type ';'
    3                | FUNCTION • error ';'

    error       shift, and go to state 4
    IDENTIFIER  shift, and go to state 5


State 2

    0 $accept: function • $end

    $end  shift, and go to state 6


State 3

    1 function: function_header • optional_variable body

    error       shift, and go to state 7
    IDENTIFIER  shift, and go to state 8

    BEGIN_  reduce using rule 13 (optional_variable)

    optional_variable  go to state 9
    variable           go to state 10


